          {
            "id": "p70-q75-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Expand ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x^2+y^2",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and use ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t=1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+y^2&=(2\\cos t+a\\sin t)^2+(\\cos t+2\\sin t)^2\\\\x^2+y^2&=5\\cos^2t+4(a+1)\\sin t\\cos t+(a^2+4)\\sin^2t.\\end{align*}$$\nFor a circle centred at the origin, this expression must be constant. Its values at $t=0$ and $t=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ must agree, and the mixed term must vanish:\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2+4&=5\\\\a^2&=1\\\\a+1&=0\\\\a&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $a=-1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+y^2&=5\\cos^2t+5\\sin^2t\\\\x^2+y^2&=5.\\end{align*}$$\nThe parametrisation is a rotation and scaling of $(\\cos t,\\sin t)$, so it traces the entire circle of radius $\\sqrt5$ for $t\\in\\mathbb R$. No points are excluded.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
